\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces  First-step logit distributions for the target emotion token, each non-target emotion token, and unrelated tokens. Unrelated tokens remain strongly suppressed across all classes, whereas specific non-target emotion tokens consistently receive elevated logits. This shows that the model's uncertainty is concentrated within the emotion subspace, where certain competing emotions are systematically preferred over others. }}{3}{figure.caption.6}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:first-step-emotion-logits}{{2}{3}{First-step logit distributions for the target emotion token, each non-target emotion token, and unrelated tokens. Unrelated tokens remain strongly suppressed across all classes, whereas specific non-target emotion tokens consistently receive elevated logits. This shows that the model's uncertainty is concentrated within the emotion subspace, where certain competing emotions are systematically preferred over others}{figure.caption.6}{}}
